
Support disclaimer: NAT capabilities depend on the router model, IOS XE release, forwarding architecture, and operating mode. Autonomous IOS XE and IOS XE SD-WAN do not necessarily support the same features or configuration syntax. This document is a broad technical reference—not a verified feature matrix for a specific router.



1. Overview

Network Address Translation—NAT—modifies IP addresses as packets traverse a router. Port Address Translation—PAT—can additionally modify TCP/UDP ports or protocol identifiers.

Common purposes include:

    Allowing private-address hosts to access external networks.
    Sharing public IPv4 addresses.
    Publishing internal services.
    Connecting networks with overlapping addresses.
    Applying different translated addresses to different destinations.
    Supporting IPv6-to-IPv4 communication through NAT64.


NAT is not a firewall. Translation does not replace access-control policies.

